# Graphify: track the current graph outputs, drop the heavy rebuildable cache,
# the local cost log, and the dated snapshots. The snapshots are a full copy of
# the graph (~10 MB) written on every rebuild, nothing reads them — no graphify
# command takes a snapshot, and no script or doc references one — and the 14 of
# them were 81 % of this repository's entire object history.
graphify-out/cache/
graphify-out/cost.json
graphify-out/20*/

# The graph and its viewer are generated: `graphify update .` rebuilds both from
# source in about five seconds with no API cost (verified 2026-08-06 from a
# clone's worth of files). Tracking an 11 MB JSON that every rebuild rewrites is
# what let a git merge corrupt it with 1,149 conflict markers. GRAPH_REPORT.md
# stays tracked -- it is small, readable in a diff, and nothing parses it.
graphify-out/graph.json
graphify-out/graph.html

# MacOS specific files
.DS_Store